# Scrollable Analysis editor header and on-demand icon picker

Refine both Analysis editors so ownership scrolls with the content and icon choices appear only when requested.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The name, editable icon, player selector, and type-specific editor content belong to one scrollable content region.
- [x] Clear, Cancel, and Save remain fixed outside that scrolling region.
- [x] Scrolling a long construction plan moves the player selector naturally with the editor content.
- [x] The current item icon appears beside the editable name.
- [x] A small pencil affordance beside the icon communicates that it can be changed.
- [x] The 3×3 icon grid is hidden by default.
- [x] Tapping the current icon or its pencil reveals the shared 3×3 icon grid.
- [x] Selecting an icon updates the draft and automatically collapses the picker without changing unrelated fields.
- [x] Production and Plan editors retain their respective cards and hammer defaults.
- [x] Cancel discards an icon change; Save persists it through TASK-033's storage path.
- [x] Editor scrolling, naming, player changes, preview placement, Clear, Cancel, and Save continue to work.
- [x] UI regression coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused layout and interaction checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Evidence

- Moved the player selector and construction preview control into the editor's scroll content.
- Placed the current icon and pencil affordance beside the name, with an animated on-demand picker that collapses after selection.
- Consolidated Clear, Cancel, and Save into the fixed bottom action bar.
- Updated UI regression coverage for the hidden/revealed/collapsed picker lifecycle.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded for app, unit-test, and UI-test bundles.
